ECHO(1)                    Funny CLI Manual                     ECHO(1)

NAME
    echo — Display text in the terminal.

SYNOPSIS
    echo <text>

DESCRIPTION
    The 'echo' command prints the provided text to the terminal.

    Multiple arguments are joined together with spaces, allowing you to
    write a complete sentence without worrying about the terminal
    understanding you.

ARGUMENTS
    text    The text to display.
    Multiple words can be provided as separate arguments.

USAGE
    > echo Hello
        Displays Hello.

    > echo Hello World
        Displays Hello World.

EXAMPLES
    > echo Welcome to the CLI
        Prints the message "Welcome to the CLI".

    > echo This is a test
        Prints the provided sentence.

    > echo
        Prints an empty line.

FUN FACTS
    - echo does not modify files.
    - Multiple arguments are automatically separated by spaces.
    - echo is one of the simplest commands in the CLI.
    - Sometimes you just need the computer to say something back.

SEE ALSO
